1170 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Alan: We were awesome last night.":GOSUB 5100:GOTO 1060
1180 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: Remind me again, who was that guy who was freaking out because he\had a bad dream about forgetting the lyrics?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1190 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Alan: That was a stupid dream anyway. The moment we stepped onto the\stage it was completely out of my mind.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1200 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: If the bus gets to Tours by tonight, we'll have a couple of days all\to ourselves.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1210 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Andrew: To be honest, we all have that kind of dream from time to time.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1220 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Andrew: If we get two days off, we should really do some sightseeing. David\got to visit Paris by night. Or at least, he did in his dreams.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1230 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: You don't get to go on a trip around Europe every day. I'd like to see\some famous landmarks in the real world, not in a dream.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1240 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: What do you say?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1250 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Martin: Count me out. I'm going to use those two days to come up with a new\song.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1260 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Alan: Eh, I don't know. I don't really care about a bunch of old places.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1270 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: This is my first big job, so I think I'm going to use the time to get\some rest.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1280 GOSUB 6110:BM$="Andrew and Alan had lowered their seats, resting. They must have been\tired from their last performance.":GOSUB 5100
1290 COMMON FO:BM$="Martin meanwhile had taken out the guitar and was arranging a new song.":GOSUB 5100
1295 GOSUB 9020:GOSUB 6140
1300 BM$="David looked outside the window while listening to the sound of Martin's\guitar.":GOSUB 5100
1310 BM$="The bus was approaching a large rocky mountain. A significant number of\people could be seen at its top.":GOSUB 5100
1315 GOSUB 5610:GOSUB 9560:GOSUB 9550:GOSUB 9540:GOSUB 9530:GOSUB 6160:GOSUB 5820
1320 BM$="David forgot when he got off the bus. He was climbing the mountain.":GOSUB 5100
1322 GOSUB 5870
1325 BM$="The man climbing the mountain was not the same David who had been on the\bus. His face and his clothes were different; however, his consciousness\had become David's.":GOSUB 5100
1327 GOSUB 6170
1330 BM$="David brushed many people aside, and kept climbing his way up.":GOSUB 5100
1340 BM$="David could no longer hear the sound of Martin's guitar. He could only\hear the wind, blowing past his ears.":GOSUB 5100
1350 BM$="A few words were going through David's mind.\`They've finally come... This shall be the final battle.`":GOSUB 5100
1360 BM$="Then he yelled:\`I shall perform the final ritual! Prepare yourselves...`":GOSUB 5100
1370 BM$="Before he could realize it, David had become an arch-mage of an ancient\civilization.":GOSUB 5100
1375 GOSUB 9545:GOSUB 6210
1380 BM$="His people raised their hands, yelling in excitement.":GOSUB 5100
1390 BM$="For the last hundred years, David's clan had been under attack by the\northern tribes. They had been cornered down, below this mountain.":GOSUB 5100
1405 BM$="The ritual he was performing would bestow them incredible power at the\cost of their lives; however, they had no other way to oppose the might of\the northern tribes.":GOSUB 5100
1406 BM$="`But if we must all die, then we shall take down as many of them as we can.`\he thought.":GOSUB 5100
1445 BM$="They all knew this would be their final stand; and yet, they kept cheering\on David, the great mage, as he completed the ritual.":GOSUB 5100
1446 GOSUB 6180:GOSUB 9555
1450 BM$="David: Laayra en'yaa maira... Sion thaanra esuno...":GOSUB 5100
1460 BM$="David began chanting his spell...":GOSUB 5100
